[{"id":"VRCE-6-93-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":1,"english":"After gradually regaining his senses, Rāvana, urged on by the force of the Finisher, getting into a furious passion, with his eyes reddened in wrath, addressed the charioteer, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.733,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"95d6435200f9e925ed24dc2d94d38e268e03433ab270a9b42df65c1c176d8a1c","compact":"3cb52964c02ad62c934159bb5e297d7cf4f6e5b7e0976067e7e5a6cbd92fa906","nasal":"3df6e63f7a67b4d72150dc62ff33ef62589a23a3e07eea4355fb19bd13dd5270"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":2,"english":"perverse sense, disregarding me as devoid of prowess, and incompetent, and bereft of vigour-as cowardly, light, nerveless and shorn of energy, and as divorced by the power of illusion and debarred by arms, you act on your own understanding.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2494dee137b7b2dc0dac027856aaa622e40c791917aac8d564439b7ee0b7e16d","compact":"68fb4b355a0f3996f0a015a0d14469faf1a4887dadb5b76a523e1873fe034fb3","nasal":"d8086d45f169a62256111adaff9c13be0b5e807399c80243953cf0e2d8584a3a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":3,"english":"perverse sense, disregarding me as devoid of prowess, and incompetent, and bereft of vigour-as cowardly, light, nerveless and shorn of energy, and as divorced by the power of illusion and debarred by arms, you act on your own understanding.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.786,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"012b10d17c6906713e1c5a26015961bb4464ab1f3c5bca5c8cf7087e57345195","compact":"371c54368a8df433b9df104faa8b484b65de0d8a8bd677930c718204b6bf287b","nasal":"21deecffa22154d80f4d801ae3392a41c2f7b9f06ad48545339deedb33b384a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":4,"english":"Wherefore disregarding me, and not minding O you of my purpose, have you taken away my car from before the presence of the enemy?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c3f9f112220eb9231f10bdc5cdce7f4f3698a5c07ba03817b5048eafad92bce3","compact":"3cab5400826afb33dd3cc03c487f30f6941911e749a8c68671d357da5bef9b28","nasal":"92c42e37a6e90586fb63986cf754d4c0be456bb61bedd6f23e928cb0bcc652cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":5,"english":"O abject one! by you have my long earned renown and energy and prowess and credit been brought to naught.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0cdba3a2ae13ed847b3af52eecce323abd05de61d390ce2698315f23f31d0811","compact":"1585373e0a7618a958e40e48767c3956f046259cd40ae8d3d453d4e1b8494ede","nasal":"1585373e0a7618a958e40e48767c3956f046259cd40ae8d3d453d4e1b8494ede"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":6,"english":"In the very sight of an enemy of renowned prowess, and one capable of being gratified with valorous deeds, have you made me, burning for battle, look as if I were a coward.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a476df2225a46b54423c6926307f48975d2f7cd64d9a4d685bc246b61424d5b9","compact":"535b9dd57e9a5320786b10aa131dbae85ab4980b111df27f5a77406c45f4d792","nasal":"893d24a9c67abc19f4fe130f91115e6dc1dd03521acc2e27599ff0b0f0d37ba5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":7,"english":"As, O wicked minded one, you did not even through heedlessness, take the car to the field of batile, I infer for certain that you have been bribed by the foe.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.508,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"046a6897d8376e30b6f5ecfb8c1cecda9cad2a06c8646cc363d17e49ac8bb881","compact":"2b2842e1c9ff2116646f3c3f288a5abeb0012d11cc7f223c4e45556bf13ffd3c","nasal":"9d0541d1458b021167c79550590e7bc3eb5c8f00f9f127e95e181f234f30549d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":8,"english":"The act that you have done, does not appear as that of a friend seeking our welfare; but today you have acted like an enemy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.379,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a772af24cbf913746afdfc24b5497922288aa2d90b56f604c353b45d58490c07","compact":"6ba85114e526b226a8b5e1a34f6cbbd86ce131dec272d0d3c4fb930b9478253b","nasal":"f201087dab7f9f1e2c3a5034719fead0c182587d35f196f3c4b63ee9dc5fe8f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":9,"english":"If you have been maintained by me, if you remember my merit, do you swiftly turn the car before my enemy has departed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.515,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b1e057e538fa69a0dd800c3e68e1110bb4c83e37acf3598c1ee965ef95435486","compact":"e3e2a06f6f6d95230eab8c84f68a959f64cd4dde71a89832320bfbb3278ed048","nasal":"fe2bf16743822a09fd9828e613127d59149bd497e342392bf0cf259579c20ab2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":10,"english":"Thus admonished by him of slender sense, the charioteer possessed of intelligence, humbly spoke to Råvaņa words fraught with good.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c61ee5043a8925bc67f476540fe4de67d3d6d73536324756e1e73b3f01585a6","compact":"1dc70c991c095bed795d6baa0b530fa768acd3b48940d4bc880d4415aeb84b16","nasal":"1dc70c991c095bed795d6baa0b530fa768acd3b48940d4bc880d4415aeb84b16"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":11,"english":"I am not afraid, nor stupefied, nor have I been bribed by the foe, nor am I negligent. And I have not forgotten your affection or your good offices.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a321933dbb24cd68ba894f45f9c73ac94d4e5e61f61545a2192e17b60a09a03","compact":"789dce2638d5bec132bccbe127996ee6bfff7cbe44474a47b0b43dd6beda671c","nasal":"789dce2638d5bec132bccbe127996ee6bfff7cbe44474a47b0b43dd6beda671c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":12,"english":"And studious of your welfare, I have saved your fame; and with a mind overflowing with affection I have done (to you) this unpalatable good.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.644,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b96cfd9f10601eea28e5c19ae7c087dd2eb3a0ee82403b950916615435f434e1","compact":"ca57ba43bc416a72ae4a6c2c715af374160131373dba6b90848777b8f094bc94","nasal":"d7d62c9129c77ccb926bb8713f1065bdcc5f29d8e39896b604fb6980da41d00c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":13,"english":"O mighty monarch, for this, you should not, like a frivolous and base one, criminate me that am ever engaged in what is good and dear to you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"baf5436dede8d90f99cc6511de142206f2caf85a85f9e0ba59505047aae886ba","compact":"653581c9ed6bdc1653a0cbbaff91a3ce3bda749845807135b7ec1a1d90a9e170","nasal":"2ef04e6daa97973c8ccc9cbbf419178cff014f18879acf5a6d2336f2e36e5985"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":14,"english":"Listen! I shall render you reason why I turned away from the field the car, rushing like a river when the sea is swelled up* *On the ascension of the Moon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.82,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"02d39592ef417042eb38d464724d43a4562d62c1e98d4b14a1f3a32f339a96b2","compact":"52012aea2a519c71a249b9a7b7f85ae5ea772879174e33a907cacbcffd04c044","nasal":"cb18a666c2bd6423ab1c8e86bc51af9f9a18ebbfa530c16351516686bafd03fa"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":15,"english":"I knew that you had been fatigued in consequence of your mighty exertions in the fight. And I could not perceive that your prowess then stood superior (to that of the foe).* *Two negatives in this verse amounting to an affirmative. This is the only instance of double negatives in Valmiki.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.623,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"478ae4b3e61357c82c2e341359c9b88180006b42103cde677ac6a203af8877ac","compact":"14619d54ed32c863d81384b3da86f3caa67c27a595a452c1f4c2ce647a40f63b","nasal":"14619d54ed32c863d81384b3da86f3caa67c27a595a452c1f4c2ce647a40f63b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":16,"english":"The steeds of my car were worn out by-carrying it; and they were battered, and helpless and perspired like kine in a shower.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.685,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4b68f13cd224e099132fc7275ea5394380d232b2774f5a9f17c3d3a692a5934a","compact":"e4b2269665f6f6baa9a5d87dd34764f0d479d8a2e09f6cdbe937c0bdaa0d93cf","nasal":"e6161c04badeebfb685ae19808adb94096cd6efc350bf95d26485f08a62673ab"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":17,"english":"And bad omens fast sprang up before us. And on these occurring, I perceived that things would go against us.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"511e91987513722885901593ad6a9c0a38306ca1afad4aea65ae91af7e09cd25","compact":"85f56aa9f35f6fdf99aba8955fa503c56b05e94b0c5d8f5194d5b409b0723166","nasal":"c61a9f54240c0e9c4d6de86cf1ba1c17b8435c6e3a09f54da3b2dbf8ddd527a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":18,"english":"O you endowed with exceeding might, a charioteer should be conversant with season and place, with omens, and the expressions of emotions; as also with depression of spirits, exhilaration, and grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d11b69eb72c2fbeaebf822d54287059f290f958e3dfcb70cf034cb16d0b3ca5e","compact":"414fe6cc5dab747d18934af299ce0a0a99cabac62fca7ff7fec5a0f4a0c49bc1","nasal":"fbf1c9151d961670521074b50f32e5cdc1ecedbbd6d4b4b7f89af8d3eb40be5c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":19,"english":"And he should have a knowledge of low, lever and uneven grounds, and the time for conflict, and he should be able to perceive the shortcomings of the enemy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"33a276008388745df83b3455dd0ab808e0ceec42180bfd32bd71b2ea10160251","compact":"fc71ccddc601a47d126425757849afaf9afd67a30c75ced3cdbdd3f5f0907874","nasal":"257dda8a3c341235bb4d4e190df63a70d61760bf08eed79d0a52b1782080d6c2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":20,"english":"And a charioteer mounted on a car, should know when to draw near an enemy, when to turn away from him when to stay; and when to turn round from before the foe-all these (he should know).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7bde6cd38cbf6929335d1514abd111e3bf5598f322235ac6220ad46f57d1de06","compact":"aee16dc39b93fcc53d9e924d03eeec1252c2947f4526f2d81d5481f04eebaf06","nasal":"e47253659ab97ece1c58e82580696fc0709c80287a0f3cddad64ce6870883c88"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":21,"english":"What I, for bringing respite to you as well as the horses of the car, have done by way of removing the terrific exhaustion, is proper.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"52c7ca4044d9aa2b61dc8692b547aeb22aca38976abe5964c0cc88ade785b961","compact":"0fbc3046f35ee7a0399059dcb382ff20d25e08d4ecf2bc9cd4235dd60c1885b2","nasal":"0fbc3046f35ee7a0399059dcb382ff20d25e08d4ecf2bc9cd4235dd60c1885b2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":22,"english":"I did not, O hero, turn away the car of my own sheer will. What I have done, O lord, had been dictated by my affection for you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.604,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d37d47315234c4610fdfc280118bbfdb164e42d5127eef8612e01a76b2f61363","compact":"995d218da2482561dd6701f1ed2741136e9c69db4b48381d0e5cb6da8c709f60","nasal":"995d218da2482561dd6701f1ed2741136e9c69db4b48381d0e5cb6da8c709f60"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":23,"english":"Command me. What you say, O destroyer of foes. I will do every way, O hero with my whole soul.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a893561f0df15523658d0377e03db23e45d88d4789c41da1213337f3b062dae2","compact":"9c63b2c571b1d59673a1030c6264b5fd6f7595e3ecc19cbf0a6c516ef26cb2ee","nasal":"9c63b2c571b1d59673a1030c6264b5fd6f7595e3ecc19cbf0a6c516ef26cb2ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":24,"english":"Thereat, well pleased with the speech of the charioteer, Ravana, eager for encounter, after praising him in various ways said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7c04d1621fb4f50bbd7b463d371f02507bedc9ed73c3195f9f4047f4a9fcdb11","compact":"89c4647265c6b32983336cb26b57af6213a581c35e500660a66f21a59a43ce8f","nasal":"89c4647265c6b32983336cb26b57af6213a581c35e500660a66f21a59a43ce8f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":25,"english":"O charioteer, do you swiftly take the car towards Rāghava. Without slaying his foe in fight, Ravana turn not away (from the field).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093025","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e7d91da4d868de928dab56b4807548d19366ab106cada5bb6d6caa78ef98cd9","compact":"2da61a15861b0bb1cd2f9cc5f98b30166b9d4946d4b715682c10d54f743e52f1","nasal":"3cdd57641b3b084201e87770efb50bda33df85563174fc611628bbf809e26490"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-26","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":26,"english":"Speaking thus Råvaņa-lord of Rākşasas-gave the charioteer on the car an excellent ornament for the hand. Hearing Ravana's words, the charioteer drove the car.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.73,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd5abab2c3006dbb483cedf31865ae39b522ef428115199f68562298c1f982e2","compact":"4648eddf3e2abbc7c79562b6f87f59276d221183368bf2270a766a006c65fe63","nasal":"4648eddf3e2abbc7c79562b6f87f59276d221183368bf2270a766a006c65fe63"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-93-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":93,"verse":27,"english":"And urged on by the speech of Rāvana, the charioteer drove on the steeds, and in a moment the mighty chariot of the Rākşasa-chief appeared before Rāma in the field of battle.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-104-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6093027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d710b784930320ab00f3bec9f3530b1487b77a3826906ccd2852bf63744eb6e8","compact":"70ad021cff9a45f7c3d822ec3bdfce5dce070b90bda0fdf1adfab7e07101d05d","nasal":"6dd07d5a8e08993a4886fb362ec76e9d5e66ed42c9879ac910c73623daf32b30"}}]
